              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "**Ukraine** (often spelled *Ukrania* or *Ucrania* in Spanish and other languages) is a country located in Eastern Europe. It is the second-largest country by area in Europe, after Russia, and its capital and largest city is **Kyiv**. \n\n### Quick Facts:\n* **Capital:** Kyiv\n* **Official Language:** Ukrainian\n* **Currency:** Hryvnia (UAH)\n* **Government:** Unitary semi-presidential republic\n\n---\n\n### Current Status & Ongoing Conflict (2026)\nSince February 2022, Ukraine has been defending itself against a full-scale invasion by Russia. \n\n* **The Frontline:** The conflict spans a frontline of nearly 800 miles. The frontlines have largely stabilized, and the war has transitioned into a highly attritional phase. \n* **Battlefield Dynamics:** Russia's spring-summer offensives have largely stalled. The Russian military's rate of advance has significantly slowed compared to previous years. At the same time, Ukraine has conducted localized counterattacks and intensified its deep, long-range strikes targeting military and logistics infrastructure inside Russian territory.\n* **High-Tech Warfare:** The conflict is highly defined by electronic and drone warfare. Ukraine's extensive use of domestically produced drones and advanced software has played a major role in halting Russian armored and infantry advances.\n* **Diplomacy & Aid:** International aid continues to support Ukraine. Meanwhile, diplomatic efforts have taken on a new focus; Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy has recently renewed calls for direct ceasefire negotiations with Russia. \n\n***\n\n*Si prefieres recibir esta informaci\u00f3n en espa\u00f1ol o deseas saber m\u00e1s sobre un tema en espec\u00edfico (como su historia, cultura, geograf\u00eda o detalles del conflicto actual), por favor d\u00edmelo.*",
